    "text": "6 hours ago COMSTOCK PARK, Mich. — Nothing says summer like a fresh, sun-warmed strawberry in early June, and this year, it’ll be a little sweeter - literally. After a rollercoaster couple of months weather-wise, Mother Nature is responding differently depending on the crop or plant that you’re looking at. For strawberries, the wild weather hasn’t had much of a negative impact. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
